-- CC_0409 — the AP zero-vote prose, corrected from each state's OWN return (43 rows, 6 states)
--
-- WHAT WAS WRONG
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- CC_0381 read AP's per-state results feed and wrote each winner's tally into result_source as
-- prose. For an UNCONTESTED race AP publishes voteCount 0 and calls the race at poll close, so
-- 55 winners were recorded in production as having won with no votes. That is false about every
-- one of them: the ballots were cast and the states counted them.
--
-- The discriminator was in the same AP file all along, one level up from the number that was
-- read: metadata.uncontested = true. Measured across all 54 rows still carrying the sentence,
-- every one of them is flagged uncontested in AP's feed — one mechanism, not several.
--
-- ⚠ uncontested does NOT by itself mean "AP publishes no count". Measured in these same feeds,
-- four uncontested U.S. House races (MA-02, MA-05, MA-07, WI-02) DO carry full tallies. The
-- condition that means "AP is not tabulating this" is uncontested = true AND voteCount = 0, and
-- in these feeds that combination is confined to state-legislative races.
--
-- WHAT THIS FILE DOES
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- For the 43 rows whose own state publishes a return today, it replaces the citation with one
-- built from that state's figures. ONE ROW, ONE COLUMN each: result, result_certainty and
-- result_recorded_at are gated UNCHANGED. The call was and remains AP's; only the count and its
-- provenance are corrected, and no row is promoted toward "certified" — every one of these
-- returns is marked unofficial by the state that published it.
--
-- 🔴 THE REMAINING 11 ARE DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED, AND THE POST-VERIFY ASSERTS EXACTLY 11.
-- Wisconsin (8) and Massachusetts (3) publish no statewide unofficial return at all, and each
-- says so in its own words:
--   WEC: "Wisconsin does not have a statewide system for reporting unofficial results on
--   Election Night, and there is no central official website or feed where results are reported
--   ... The unofficial statewide and county results numbers that the public sees ... come from
--   the news media, including the Associated Press, which collects them from the 72 county
--   clerks' websites." (elections.wi.gov/election-results, read 2026-11-12)
--   MA SoC: "We do not publish unofficial election results ... local officials don't report
--   unofficial results to the state." Cities and towns have 15 days after a state election to
--   certify. (sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/voting-information/announcing-certifying.htm,
--   read 2026-11-12)
-- Those 11 need county and municipal clerks and are a separate, later pass. Correcting them
-- here would mean inventing a state source that does not exist.
--
-- SOURCES READ, ALL ON 2026-11-12
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--   Washington (19 rows) — Washington Secretary of State, 2026 General Election returns (results.votewa.gov/results/public/api/elections/washington/20261103/data)
--   Arizona (11 rows) — Arizona Secretary of State, 2026 General Election returns (app.enhancedvoting.com/results/public/api/elections/Arizona/110326GeneralElection/data, linked as the official unofficial results from results.arizona.vote)
--   Utah (7 rows) — Utah Lieutenant Governor / state election results, 2026 General Election (electionresults.utah.gov/results/public/api/elections/Utah/General11032026/data)
--   California (4 rows) — California Secretary of State, 2026 General Election returns (api.sos.ca.gov/returns/state-assembly/district/N)
--   Colorado (1 row) — Colorado Secretary of State, 2026 General Election night reporting (results.enr.clarityelections.com/CO/127407/386814/json/en/summary.json)
--   Oregon (1 row) — Oregon Secretary of State, 2026 General Election returns (results.oregonvotes.gov/resultsSW.aspx?type=HOUSE&map=CTY, districts 31-60)
--
-- ⚠ Arizona moved its 2026 general OFF results.arizona.vote; the SoS's own results page links to
-- the Enhanced Voting host used above, which is why that host is the state's return and not a
-- third party's. Washington and Utah publish through the same vendor and the same JSON shape.
--
-- POSITIVE CONTROLS ON THE READS (so that "one candidate" is a fact about the ballot, not the parser)
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
--   WA 140 of 173 contests list more than one named candidate; AZ 96 of 99; UT 122 of 135;
--   CO 55 of 65 State Representative contests; CA 8 of 8 sampled Assembly districts.
--   A file that could only ever yield one candidate per contest would have made every row here
--   look uncontested whatever the truth.
-- ⚠ WRITE-IN PRACTICE DIFFERS BY STATE AND SILENCE IS NOT EVIDENCE. WA (155/173) and AZ (76/99)
--   publish write-in lines and those totals are quoted below. UT (3 of 135), CO (0 of 65) and CA
--   (0 of 12 sampled) publish none, so their citations say the state lists no write-in line
--   rather than claiming the winner took 100%.
-- ⚠ NONE of these states sets a winner flag on these contests (CO sets none on any of its 302).
--   The count is the state's; the call stays AP's. Two facts, labelled separately.
--
-- PRIOR VALUES
-- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- 🔴 An UPDATE is final here: there is no history table and no ordered runner, so the overwritten
-- text exists nowhere once this commits. Every prior value is carried BELOW, in prior_source,
-- beside the md5 it must hash to. Gate 0 refuses the file if the recorded text does not match its
-- recorded hash; gate 1 refuses unless the LIVE column hashes to the same thing. The record is
-- therefore checked against production rather than asserted in a comment.

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE cc0409_rows (
  rc_id         uuid PRIMARY KEY,
  prior_md5     text    NOT NULL,
  prior_source  text    NOT NULL,   -- verbatim, the value this file overwrites
  state_votes   integer NOT NULL,   -- the number that state printed
  new_source    text    NOT NULL
) ON COMMIT DROP;

INSERT INTO cc0409_rows (rc_id, prior_md5, prior_source, state_votes, new_source) VALUES
